# Worktree contract

One session, one checkout, one branch. Parallel work on a shared repository
happens in separate git worktrees, never in one shared checkout, and never
directly on main. This rule binds every agent session in every harness; plan
templates are not the only trigger.

1. Preflight: run `git worktree list` before editing in any repository where
   another session may be active. Those are your siblings' claims.
2. Claim: `git worktree add -b feature/<slug>-<shortid> ../<slug>-<shortid> main`.
   Unique suffix always; if the path or branch is taken, pick another.
3. Stay inside your worktree; a shared checkout on main is read-only
   reference, not a workspace.
4. Managed worktrees win: if the harness placed you in a worktree (T3 Code
   thread handoff, worker checkout), use it as-is. Never nest your own.
5. Respect siblings: never modify, delete, or prune another session's
   worktree, branch, or files. Report strays, leave them.
6. Retire: merge or explicitly abandon, then `git worktree remove` and
   delete unmerged branches you created. No orphans from your session.
